title: Errand
---
Father sets down his mug and looks at you over the rim. #line:errand_000
Father: It's your sister's birthday, and I've no coin to spare for a present. But you've two hands and a good heart. #line:errand_001
Father: Do a good turn for someone in the village and they'll likely pay you for it. Earn enough, and buy Ros something from Old Garrick's stall. #line:errand_002
-> I'll do it! I'll get her the best present ever. #line:errand_opt_eager
    <<set_label attitude eager>>
    Father ruffles your hair. #line:errand_ack_eager_0
    Father: That's my child. Off you go, then. #line:errand_ack_eager
-> Do I have to? Can't Mother just buy something? #line:errand_opt_reluctant
    <<set_label attitude reluctant>>
    Father raises an eyebrow. #line:errand_ack_reluctant_0
    Father: A gift you earn means more. Go on, before I find you chores instead. #line:errand_ack_reluctant
===
